stdout.ndjson:\n  Line 5: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1774356742824,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2e01952b9ffeUgYNCBwaokJy4V\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d1fe6fdf6001kQzN5lnToVohTF\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2e01952b9ffeUgYNCBwaokJy4V\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d1fe6bfcf001uOy8M030yhKZhu\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Here’s a solid first `SKILL.md` draft:\\n\\n```md\\n---\\nname: release-note-curator\\ndescription: Curate release notes from commits, pull requests, changelogs, issue trackers, or version diffs into clear, audience-appropriate summaries. Use this skill whenever the user wants to draft, rewrite, polish, categorize, shorten, or expand release notes, GitHub release text, changelog entries, \\\"what shipped\\\" updates, upgrade summaries, or launch highlights—even if they do not explicitly say \\\"release notes.\\\"\\ncompatibility:\\n  tools: [read, glob, grep, bash]\\n---\\n\\n# Release Note Curator\\n\\nCreate accurate, well-structured release notes from source material such as commit history, merged PRs, changelog fragments, issue summaries, docs, or diffs between versions.\\n\\nThe goal is not to restate raw development activity. The goal is to help the user communicate what changed, why it matters, and what the intended audience should know.\\n\\n## Trigger guidance\\n\\nUse this skill when the user asks for things like:\\n\\n- \\\"Draft release notes for v1.6.0\\\"\\n- \\\"Turn these merged PRs into a GitHub release summary\\\"\\n- \\\"Summarize what shipped this week\\\"\\n- \\\"Write customer-facing notes from this changelog\\\"\\n- \\\"Create upgrade notes from the diff between these tags\\\"\\n- \\\"Rewrite these release notes to be clearer / shorter / more polished\\\"\\n- \\\"Group these changes into features, fixes, and breaking changes\\\"\\n\\nStrong trigger signals include:\\n\\n- Mentions of release notes, changelogs, GitHub releases, launch summaries, version highlights, or upgrade notes\\n- Requests to summarize commits, PRs, or issue lists for humans\\n- Requests to transform technical change history into customer-facing or stakeholder-friendly language\\n- Requests to reorgan...\n\n/home/hans/dev/github/opencode-coder/docs/testing/opencode-coder-a1p.6-skill-creator-smoke-2026-03-24.md:\n  Line 24: 7. `bun run test:manual -- --mode=command --fixture=existing-active-project --plugin-source=local-build -- opencode run \"Improve this existing skill after review feedback. Existing skill summary: trigger='when user asks to summarize commits', instructions are verbose and tool-specific, examples are generic. Feedback: too narrow, overfits git repos, does not explain why choices are made, and has no non-goals. Rewrite the skill and briefly explain your improvement reasoning using principles from How to think about improvements (generalization, lean prompt, and explicit why).\"`\n\n/home/hans/dev/github/opencode-coder/.manual-test-runs/run-UQGiKJ/isolated-opencode/xdg-data/opencode/log/2026-03-24T122519.log:\n  Line 1: INFO  2026-03-24T12:25:19 +499ms service=default version=1.3.0 args=[\"run\",\"Improve this existing skill after review feedback. Existing skill summary: trigger='when user asks to summarize commits', instructions are verbose and tool-specific, examples are generic. Feedback: too narrow, overfits git repos, does not explain why choices are made, and has no non-goals. Rewrite the skill and briefly explain your improvement reasoning using principles from How to think about improvements (generalization, lean prompt, and explicit why).\"] opencode","title":"trigger=.*summarize commits|summarize commits","metadata":{"matches":5,"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1774362027259,"end":1774362027430}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":""}}}}
